let __v_839 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"I'm so sorry. Wanting it back is not the same as having done it wrong, and it is the last call anyone wants to make. When you feel up to it the vet can arrange the cremation or a home burial, and you can ask them for a paw print.\",\"I'm sorry. That is the heaviest kind of decision to be carrying. You do not have to sort anything today; when you are ready the vet will handle the cremation, and they can take a paw print for you.\",\"I'm really sorry. Regret is what love looks like afterwards, and it does not mean you got it wrong. The practical bit can wait a day or two - the vet arranges the cremation, and ask them about a paw print if you would want one.\"]}")?;
frame.store("PUT_DOWN_REGRET_REPLIES", __v_839.clone())?;
let __v_840 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"I'm so sorry to hear that. It's a hard thing to carry — I'm here if you want to talk about it, or if anything practical would help.\",\"I'm really sorry. Be gentle with yourself today, and tell me if there's anything you want to talk through.\",\"That's such sad news, I'm sorry. Some days will be heavier than others — I'm here if you want to talk about it, or about anything else.\",\"I'm sorry, that's a real loss. Take today slowly, and shout if there's anything I can help you sort out.\"]}")?;
frame.store("LOSS_REPLIES", __v_840.clone())?;
let __v_841 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Say the plain things while they can hear them: that you love them, one memory you both laugh at, and that you will be all right. Nothing clever is needed.\",\"Skip the big speech and tell them one specific thing you are grateful for. It is easier to say than \\\"I love you\\\" out loud, and it is what people remember being told.\",\"Ask them what they want to talk about, and follow that. If they want the ordinary stuff - the garden, the football - that is not avoiding it, that is the visit.\",\"Bring them something to decide or to hear: how the family is, what the doctor said, the small gossip. Being useful is how most people say it.\"]}")?;
frame.store("DYING_SAY_REPLIES", __v_841.clone())?;
let __v_842 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Grieving someone who is still here is normal, and it is not a rehearsal for the real thing: it is the real thing, starting early. It comes in waves in the same way.\",\"That heaviness before the death is common - it is called anticipatory grief, and it does not make the later grief smaller or bigger, it is just its own thing. Talk to someone about it.\",\"It is normal to be tired, snappy and forgetful while someone is dying, and it is not a failing. If it is stopping you sleeping or eating for more than a fortnight, tell your GP.\",\"You can be grieving and relieved and guilty in the same hour, and none of that makes you bad. Most people who are where you are say the same.\"]}")?;
frame.store("DYING_GRIEF_REPLIES", __v_842.clone())?;
let __v_843 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"One piece at a time is the only way anyone does it. Pick the next thing - a shower, a sandwich, one phone call - and let the rest wait until that is done.\",\"Keep the shape of the day: up at the usual time, food at the usual times, bed at night. The routine carries you on the days you cannot carry yourself.\",\"Tell one person how you are actually doing today and let them do one job for you. Most people want to help and do not know how to ask.\",\"The first days are the hardest and they are not a forecast of the rest. If you cannot eat or sleep, or you cannot see a way forward, tell your GP - they can help with that.\"]}")?;
frame.store("GETTING_THROUGH_REPLIES", __v_843.clone())?;
let __v_844 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"An hour at a time, and the ordinary things - food, a shower, going to work - are not a break from it, they are how you keep going.\",\"Take one day's jobs and no more, tell people what is happening so it is not all on you, and let the visits that do not matter drop.\",\"You do not have to be all right while this is going on. If you cannot sleep or eat, or you are carrying it with nobody to say it to, tell your GP.\"]}")?;
frame.store("GETTING_THROUGH_DYING_REPLIES", __v_844.clone())?;
let __v_845 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Do it smaller rather than skip it: the same lunch or the same cake, with one or two people, and say out loud why you are having it. A day you have planned for is easier than one that just arrives.\",\"Keep the ritual and shrink it: the food they loved, their place at the table, and one story about them told to whoever is there. Doing something is what marks the day.\",\"Pick one thing to do at the time you would normally have spent together - the lunch, a walk, a visit - and tell someone you are doing it, so you are not carrying it on your own.\",\"Cook their dish or get their favourite in, and raise a glass to them: the point is to mark the day on purpose instead of letting it hit you sideways.\",\"Make the day about them: the meal they would have chosen, the people they liked, and the one thing you would have told them. If it all feels too heavy, do a small version and stop there.\"]}")?;
frame.store("REMEMBER_REPLIES", __v_845.clone())?;
let __v_846 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Tell a member of staff straight away — shops can call it out over the tannoy and watch the doors, which beats searching on your own.\",\"Go back to the last place you saw them and tell the nearest member of staff what they're wearing, so everyone is looking for the same person.\",\"Ask staff to put a call out and cover the exits. If it's a child, or someone vulnerable, ring 999 once it's more than a few minutes.\"]}")?;
frame.store("MISLAID_REPLIES", __v_846.clone())?;
let __v_847 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Keep it plain and warm: \\\"I'm so sorry\\\". Use the person's name, don't rush to fill the silence, and offer one concrete thing — a lift, a meal, covering a shift.\",\"You don't need the perfect words. \\\"I'm so sorry\\\" and then listening is most of it; add one specific offer of help this week.\",\"Say you're sorry, name them if you can, and offer something practical. \\\"I'll bring dinner on Thursday\\\" helps far more than \\\"let me know if you need anything\\\".\"]}")?;
frame.store("SAY_REPLIES", __v_847.clone())?;
